That paniclog is most likely caused by the game getting confused by
the debris of the earlier crash; errors in obj_move_timers() are going
to be a symptom rather than a cause of anything.

Have you successfully reached, say, the Castle since the first
occurrence _without_ a crash? Could you try wizard mode and hop down
the dungeon level-to-level to see if it crashes again? My suspicion
here is a corrupted nhdat file causing the game to choke on the
creation of the Medusa level, but it'd be good to know if it's
reproducible.

(The corrupted file could also be record; Medusa's relatively unusual
in that it reads the record file to glean names for its statues, but
so do graveyards for their corpses, so I'd expect the problem to have
occurred earlier. (And cockatrice nests for _their_ statues, but
that's not quite as frequent an occurrence.))

